2,1,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,We should prioritize actual user experience. I want to know if previous projects actually met the needs of the people using them.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We must also consider how construction affects the daily schedule and whether the resulting spaces are actually utilized efficiently.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A charming sentiment, Victoria. However, I am more concerned with the phantom deadlines that haunt our projects. We need to see why schedules slip.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I'm worried about the money! Do the budgets we approve actually cover the real costs? I want to see the actual tender records.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"While you all chase ghosts and pennies, you're forgetting the people actually keeping this place running. I'm interested in the burden on our staff.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, cost is important, but a cheap building that nobody likes is a waste of money. We need a balance of utility and budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if we only look at why schedules slip, we might ignore the fact that the rooms are unusable for months during the work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely why we should examine the site diaries. Weather is a convenient excuse, but the truth usually lies in the delivery schedules.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"I just don't want us to get surprised by a huge bill after the project is ""finished."" Let's look at the renewal reserves too.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, ""utility"" is a vague word. I'm talking about the grueling manual routines that never seem to get automated or improved.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I agree that staff burden is a form of utility. If the staff are struggling, the facility is failing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I think we should look at the booking data. It will tell us if the ""high demand"" claims in the proposals are actually true.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall look into the delivery schedules and the site diaries. I'd prefer our next project not to be a lesson in optimism.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll stick with the tender records and the renewal reserves. I want to see the gap between the plan and the reality.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take the staffing posts and the bench technicians' routines. Let's see exactly how many people are doing the work of ten.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,I will focus on the post-occupancy review ratings and the survey findings in the older blocks to see where we failed before.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I will investigate the timetable records on rooms out of service and the booking data for specialist and general rooms.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
