60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate A is the most flexible, but Candidate B offers a specialized utility that could serve many departments if managed openly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate A is the safest for the timetable. It uses an ""underused"" hall, meaning no displacement of existing classes or expensive rentals.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate C is a disaster waiting to happen. Outdoor work in this climate? I can already see the schedule slipping into next year.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate D is the most expensive in terms of plant equipment. Given the tender trends I saw, the budget for D is likely a huge underestimate.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate D is the only one that actually addresses the technician's burden. The ventilation and layout are exactly where the manual labor is concentrated.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I understand the need for D, but the survey findings in older blocks suggest that ground-floor work often hits hazardous materials, causing huge delays.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I must object to D on the grounds of the timetable. Closing the shared teaching labs would be a catastrophe for the coming year.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,@Victoria is correct. D is high risk. A is an indoor conversion of an underused space. It is the most rational choice for a timely delivery.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Benjamin. A is low-cost and low-risk. B involves a lot of AV equipment, and as I found, we have no reserve for its future maintenance.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the ""catastrophe"" is that our staff are currently doing the work of machines. A study commons is a luxury; functional labs are a necessity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I sympathize, but we cannot ignore the user satisfaction data. A flexible, open space like A serves the most people and avoids the ""niche"" failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we choose D, we will be paying for off-site lab space for months. The booking data shows we have no spare capacity to absorb that.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Let's be honest: D is a project that will be ""squeezed"" into the final weeks of the year after the ventilation contractors fail to show up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"And the cost of D will balloon. I'll vote for A. It's a simple conversion, the costs are predictable, and it doesn't rely on expensive plant equipment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,You're all choosing the path of least resistance. It's a classic administrative move: build a lounge and ignore the crumbling infrastructure.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It's not about resistance, Shunichi, it's about sustainable utility. A serves the students and staff without risking the budget or the schedule.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I'll vote for A. It protects the timetable, utilizes an underused space, and meets the high demand for general-purpose study areas.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. A is the only option that doesn't invite a scheduling nightmare. It is the most logical and elegant solution.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm with the group on A. It's the only one where the approved budget is likely to survive contact with the market.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for D. I'd rather be the only one fighting for the people who actually keep this university functioning.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
